abstract: >-
  Tract-level analysis of household energy burden in Chicago using the U.S.
  Department of Energy LEAD Tool (2022) and the American Community Survey:
  hotspot detection, spatial Durbin and multiscale geographically weighted
  regression, robustness and measurement-error checks, and policy analysis.
  James Rocco Quantitative Data Research Scholarship, Lake Forest College.
keywords:
  - energy burden
  - spatial econometrics
  - Chicago
  - LEAD Tool
  - MGWR
  - energy justice
